est infrastructure projects in modern history. The new set of locks allowed the transit of Neo-Panamax vessels, which are nearly three times the capacity of the older Panamax ships. This change had profound effects on global shipping routes. Previously, many goods from Asia destined for the U.S. East Coast were offloaded at West Coast ports and transported by rail. With the expansion, direct all-water routes became economically viable, leading to a shift in cargo flows. Ports on the U.S. East Coast, such as Savannah and Charleston, invested heavily in deepening harbors and upgrading cranes to handle the larger ships. Meanwhile, some West Coast ports experienced a temporary decline in market share. The expansion also impacted other regions: ports in Latin America and the Caribbean vied to become transshipment hubs. While the project was initially controversial due to cost overruns and environmental concerns, its completion has reshaped maritime trade patterns and reinforced the canal's strategic importance.1c:[\"$\",\"li\",\"09f603cd-984d-520e-97a9-4b3cc4c28eb0\",{\"id\":\"item-5\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"border-line bg-white p-[22px] shadow-card rounded-lg border\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2.5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":true,\"className\":\"font-heading flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-ink-strong font-bold text-white h-6 w-6 text-[0.78rem]\",\"children\":5}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-heading text-[1.1rem] font-extrabold text-ink\",\"children\":\"Panama Canal Expansion Effects\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"ml-auto flex flex-wrap gap-1.5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-1.5 border leading-none whitespace-nowrap\",\"data-accent\":\"neutral\",\"data-tone\":\"none\",\"style\":{\"background\":\"#ffffff\",\"borderColor\":\"#cbd5e1\",\"borderRadi