for these geographic patterns. Alexander von Humboldt, in the early 1800s, observed that widely separated regions have structurally and functionally similar vegetation if their climates are similar. Alphonse de Candolle hypothesized that latitudinal zones of tropical, temperate, and arctic vegetation are caused by temperature and in 1874 proposed formal vegetation zones with associated temperature limits.21:[\"$\",\"li\",\"8f43ae64-d37d-4350-9f90-853cc2107e99\",{\"id\":\"item-10\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"border-line bg-white p-[22px] shadow-card rounded-lg border\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2.5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":true,\"className\":\"font-heading flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-ink-strong font-bold text-white h-6 w-6 text-[0.78rem]\",\"children\":10}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-heading text-[1.1rem] font-extrabold text-ink\",\"children\":\"Ecology Climatology Study\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"ml-auto flex flex-wrap gap-1.5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-1.5 border leading-none whitespace-nowrap\",\"data-accent\":\"neutral\",\"data-tone\":\"none\",\"style\":{\"background\":\"#ffffff\",\"borderColor\":\"#cbd5e1\",\"borderRadius\":6,\"boxShadow\":\"inset 3px 0 0 #94a3b8\",\"color\":\"#475569\",\"fontSize\":\"0.72rem\",\"fontWeight\":600,\"height\":22,\"letterSpacing\":\"0.01em\",\"paddingLeft\":9,\"paddingRight\":6},\"children\":[234,\" words\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-1.5 border leading-none whitespace-nowrap\",\"data-accent\":\"$undefined\",\"data-tone\":\"success\",\"style\":{\"background\":\"#ecfdf5\",\"borderColor\":\"#6ee7b7\",\"borderRadius\":6,\"boxShadow\":\"$undefined\",\"color\":\"#065f46\",\"fontSize\":\"0.72rem\",\"fontWeight\":700,\"height\":22,\"letterSpaci